<%- include('./partials/header') %>
<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="columns">
      <div class="column m-5">
        <img
          src="/img/profile_pic.png"
          alt="Brian A. McGuire, Founder and Owner of M-Tac Trucking Compliance"
          class="image"
          style="border-radius: 0.5rem; box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1) 0px 4px 12px;"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="column m-5">
        <p class="title has-text-dark">Speaker Bio - Brian A. McGuire</p>
        <p class="subtitle has-text-dark mt-3">Founder and Owner</p>
        <p class="fs-5 pb-4 mb-0">
          Brian A. McGuire is the founder and owner of M-Tac Trucking Compliance, a full-service
          consulting firm specializing in USDOT, FMCSA, and PHMSA regulatory compliance. With more
          than 25 years of public safety experience, including a distinguished career with the New Jersey
          State Police, he is widely recognized for his practical, field-tested expertise in commercial motor
          vehicle enforcement and safety management.
          <br /><br />
          During his law enforcement career, Mr. McGuire served as a certified Commercial Vehicle
          Inspector (NASI Parts A and B) with General Hazardous Materials and Passenger Vehicle
          certifications. He conducted more than 4,000 commercial motor vehicle inspections and over
          1,000 New Entrant Safety Audits, helping carriers achieve and maintain compliance with federal
          regulations. He also completed advanced USDOT Safety Investigator and Compliance Review
          training and performed multiple compliance reviews prior to his retirement.
          <br /><br />
          Since founding M-Tac Trucking Compliance in 2019, Mr. McGuire has provided compliance
          consulting, audit preparation, and customized training to motor carriers across the country. He
          specializes in operational evaluations, safety management planning, and regulatory defense,
          helping carriers comply with Title 49 CFR Parts 171-180 and 303-399. His approach centers on
          implementing the Safety Management Cycle to build sustainable, safety-focused operations.
          <br /><br />
          Mr. McGuire is an Associate Member of the Commercial Vehicle Safety Alliance (CVSA) and
          serves on the Audits and Investigations, Enforcement and Industry Modernization, and Training
          Committees. He is the recipient of the 2020 Howard Card Safety Award from the New Jersey
          Propane Gas Association.
          <br /><br />
          A sought-after speaker and trainer, Mr. McGuire delivers practical, real-world insights on
          regulatory compliance, safety management systems, hazardous materials transportation, and
          audit preparation.
        </p>
        <div class="columns mt-5 is-centered is-variable is-4">
          <div class="column is-half-tablet is-half-desktop">
            <div class="card has-background-light has-text-dark">
              <div class="card-content is-flex is-flex-direction-column is-align-items-center">
                <figure class="image pb-3">
                  <img
                    src="/img/njpga.png"
                    class="is-round"
                    alt="NJPGA"
                    style="height: 80px; width: auto;"
                  />
                </figure>
                <p class="title is-6 has-text-centered has-text-dark">
                  2020 NJ Propane Gas Association Safety Award Recipient
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="column is-half-tablet is-half-desktop">
            <div class="card has-background-light has-text-dark">
              <div class="card-content is-flex is-flex-direction-column is-align-items-center">
                <figure class="image pb-2">
                  <img
                    src="/img/csva.png"
                    class="is-round"
                    alt="CVSA"
                    style="height: 80px; width: auto;"
                  />
                </figure>
                <p class="title is-6 has-text-centered has-text-dark">
                  Associate member of the Commercial Vehicle Safety Alliance (CVSA)
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
